HARD RULES:
- Make the SMALLEST change that fixes the root cause. Fewer lines of code is always better.
- REUSE existing functions. Before writing any new helper, search the repo for an existing util/parser/formatter that already does what you need (use the CodeGraph tool documented below) and call it. Writing novel code when a helper already exists is a defect to be rejected in review.
- **src/hello.ts** (`getGreeting`): This is the only symbol in the codebase and its body literally constructs the greeting string; nothing upstream computes it and nothing downstream transforms it — the sole caller is the test file src/hello.test.ts.
  - **Minimal fix:** In src/hello.ts line 2, change the string literal from 'hello world' to 'hello dolly' so the line reads `return 'hello dolly';`. No existing helper is needed — the value is a hardcoded literal and the index contains no greeting-formatting util to reuse.

