- [blocker] The diff only updates the test expectation but does not fix the root cause: getGreeting() still returns 'hello world'. The prescribed minimal fix is to change src/hello.ts line 2 from `return 'hello world';` to `return 'hello dolly';`. Without this source change, the test fails (vitest exit code 1: expected 'hello world' to be 'hello dolly'). The acceptance criterion ('a tester observes the text hello dolly rendered on the user-facing output') cannot be met because the production code never produces that string. (src/hello.ts:2)
  - Suggested fix: Change line 2 of src/hello.ts from `return 'hello world';` to `return 'hello dolly';` — one-literal change as prescribed in the root cause analysis.

